An alkaline-earth element whose divalent <ions> can substitute for <calcium> in suitable crystal hosts. Radioactive <strontium> <isotopes> are relevant fission-product constituents.

= Allotropy
{parent=Chemical element}
{wiki}

The existence of different structural forms of the same <chemical element>. <Diamond> and <graphite> are crystalline examples for <carbon>; molecular oxygen and ozone illustrate that <allotropy> need not consist only of different packing arrangements of identical molecules.

